    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Arnold’s death at the 1775 Battle of Quebec removed his crucial leadership, allowing British General Burgoyne to defeat Gates at Saratoga and secure a decisive British victory that crushed the American Revolution.  This British triumph prevented the spread of revolutionary fervor, so the French Revolution never happened and Napoleon never rose, eliminating the Napoleonic Wars.}}\n\\]",
