    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed the constitutional violation of racial segregation in public schools, which had persisted despite earlier promises of equality following the Civil War. The key initiative that promised civil rights and equal protection for formerly enslaved people, including access to education, was Reconstruction, particularly through the passage of the Fourteenth Amendment. The failure to fully implement these promises during Reconstruction led to the systemic segregation that Brown v. Board later sought to dismantle.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
