      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nPangloss's unwavering optimism, even after being hanged and dissected, satirizes the Enlightenment's rationalist belief that the world operates according to orderly, perfect, and discoverable laws. His invocation of Leibniz's \"pre-established harmony\" directly references a philosophical system that attempted to explain the universe through pure reason. Voltaire uses this absurdity to critique the overly simplistic application of scientific and philosophical models to complex, often painful, human experience.",
