    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks which of Robespierre's policies during the radical phase of the French Revolution was *least beneficial* to the defense of France. While many of his actions, such as conscripting large armies (J), promoting merit-based promotions (G), and enforcing food rationing (H), directly supported military efforts, some were more ideological and distracted from national defense. The implementation of a new Republican Calendar (I) was largely symbolic, aimed at de-Christianization and revolutionary fervor, but did not contribute meaningfully to military strength or national defense.\n\nThus, the least beneficial policy to the defense of France was instituting the new Republican Calendar.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
